  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A solid metal sphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> having charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is enclosed inside the concentric spherical shell of inner radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and outer radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in the figure. The approximate variation electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, as a function of distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>, from centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>, is given by:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0134_966c633706fd.png\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 257px;\" /></p>"
